 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34CL c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2010Do03:                          
 34CL2c  Nucl. Instr. and Meth. A 613, 218 (2010)                               
 34CL c  Compiled by: G. G~urdal (ANL), February 17,2010                        
 34CL c  {+37}Ca|)3p+{+34}Cl via secondary fragmentation on {+9}Be target.      
 34CL c  2010Do03: The excited states of {+34}Cl were populated using a two     
 34CL2c  step fragmentation reaction. A primary beam of                         
 34CL3c  {+40}Ca at an energy of 420MeV/u was provided by the heavy ion         
 34CL4c  synchrotron SIS at GSI and impinged on a {+9}Be target with 4 mg/cm{+2}
 34CL5c  thickness. From the primary reaction products {+37}Ca was selected and 
 34CL6c  incident on a 700 mg/cm{+2} secondary {+9}Be target at 195.7 MeV/u to  
 34CL7c  populate the excited levels of {+34}Cl following a secondary three     
 34CL8c  proton removal reaction. RISING setup consisting of fragment separator 
 34CL9c  (FRS), 15 Cluster HPGe detectors, eight MINIBALL HPGe detectors and    
 34CL2c  eight Hector BaF{-2} detectors is used. The energy spread of the heavy 
 34CL3c  ions in front of the secondary target is measured by the time-of-flight
 34CL4c  between two scintillator detectors. The outgoing particle direction and
 34CL5c  the reaction point are determined via position sensitive Si detectors. 
 34CL6c  Measured: E|g, I|g, T{-1/2} (from lineshape of the |g-ray transition   
 34CL7c  after applying Doppler correction and comparing to simulations)        
